From: Raxcoms <mpaulo968@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gamescope: add hooks for an optional external color provider

Load an AutoHDR provider through one versioned C interface
(gamescope-color-provider.h). The provider owns inverse tone mapping,
content eligibility, colour plans, presentation sequencing and scanout
retries; gamescope supplies plain facts and performs operations on its
own resources through synchronous callbacks. An absent, incompatible or
failed provider keeps the native path.

The provider's mapping is applied through gamescope's existing LUT
builder, after SDR gamut mapping and before gain, white adaptation and
output encoding, into an extra LUT pair that only the converted game
layer selects: on the plane colour pipelines (0045) for direct scanout,
and in the composite shader otherwise. SDR overlays keep their own
tables. No GPU pass is added. Enabled by the ConVar auto_hdr (default
off; e.g. gamescope_auto_hdr=1 in the environment, or gamescopectl).

RE-ROLLED from armada PR #843 (gamescope 0035) onto novadeck's stack:
- the provider library is libnovadeck-autohdr.so.2 and the ConVar
  auto_hdr (armada: libarmada-autohdr.so.2, armada_auto_hdr);
- the interface header is carried in src/ and included with quotes,
  instead of being installed by a separate development package;
- the DRM-lease conditions (g_sDrmLeaseClientSocket, leasedPlaneIds) are
  dropped: novadeck carries no DRM lease support, so no plane is leased;
- create_color_mgmt_luts() keeps novadeck 0014's scanout-scale
  out-parameter, with the provider's colour plan after it;
- 0045 already carries the resume fix, so only the provider-aware table
  selection is new in drm_set_plane_luts().
